course: dictionary
lesson: 3580
title: Fez: a hat and a city
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A fez is a round red felt hat with a flat top, a black tassel, and no brim. It is traditional in Turkey, North Africa and the Middle East.
explain: Fez with a capital F is a famous old city in Morocco. Read the words around it to find out which one is meant. «Yasmin says the oldest university is in Fez, Morocco; Tom says Oxford.» Morocco and university are clues: a city fits, but a hat does not.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it in. «Tom says Oxford» works with a city, because Oxford is a place too, so Fez must be a place here. Context clues are your best tool for words with more than one meaning.
fact: A fez is a noun, and its plural is fezzes.
fact: With a small f, fez means a hat. With a capital F, Fez means a city in Morocco.
fact: In history lessons, the fez was worn in the Ottoman Empire until Turkey banned it in 1925.
fact: Today the fez is often a fun costume hat in stories and on TV, and magicians sometimes wear one.
fact: «Wear a fez» is a phrase you can use when you mean putting the hat on your head.
exercise: «He put on a red fez for the school play.» What is a fez? | A tall umbrella with a flat top | *A round red felt hat with a flat top and a black tassel | A pair of red shoes | A kind of red felt blanket
exercise: Yasmin says «the oldest university is in Fez, Morocco». What kind of place is Fez here? | A kind of tassel | A round red hat | *A famous old city in Morocco | A shop that sells felt
exercise: In history, the fez was worn in the Ottoman Empire. Which country banned it in 1925? | Scotland | *Turkey | Egypt | Australia
test: What colour is the tassel on a fez? | Gold | *Black | White | Red
test: «Al-Qarawiyyin in Fez was founded in 859 by a woman, Fatima al-Fihri.» In which year was it founded? | *859 | 1925 | 1859 | 1958
exam: In «Yasmin says the oldest university is in Fez, Morocco», what does Fez mean? | A round red felt hat | A black tassel | A university in Oxford | *A famous old city in Morocco
